## Failure root cause (run 43992956445) — a latent PRODUCTION gap, not just CI config
Failing tests (internal/wormhole): TestPushRecoversFromConcurrentRemoteUpdate, TestReadOnlyMultiCycleImport, TestDaemonRestartMultiCycleReadOnly — all with:
  fatal: empty ident name (for <runner@...>) not allowed / Committer identity unknown (during "git rebase")
Code evidence (master e060e2e / branch):
- internal/wormhole/git_sync.go:342-352 `gitCommandEnv()` passes os.Environ() through (minus LC_ALL) and adds only LC_ALL=C + GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0 — **no identity**.
- git_sync.go:503-510 `commitAtLocked()` adds `-c user.name=starfleetctl -c user.email=starfleetctl@localhost` → commits are self-contained.
- `rebaseLocked()` (git_sync.go:403+) calls gitLocked("rebase", ...) **without** those flags → on any machine without a global git identity (bare CI runner, minimal container), the push-recovery rebase fails.
Locally this is masked by the developer's global git config (user.name=Enrico Weigelt …), which is why the suite passed in my ship shell.
Consequence for the fleet: wormhole push recovery (non-fast-forward rebase) breaks on any host without a preconfigured git identity. Reported to Voyager (implementation owner of the wormhole branch); suggested fix: give rebaseLocked the same -c user.* flags as commitAtLocked, or set GIT_AUTHOR_*/GIT_COMMITTER_* in gitCommandEnv().

## Workflow fix (commit b83596139c49fc0837220890bfab02d14bd2ca1c)
The test step now sets GIT_AUTHOR_NAME/EMAIL and GIT_COMMITTER_NAME/EMAIL (starfleetctl CI <ci@starfleetctl.local>), so CI is deterministic and independent of runner git config. Verified locally with git configs disabled: the three previously failing tests pass (ok internal/wormhole 14.367s). YAML re-validated.

